{"type":"standard","title":"Mike McGuire (politician)","displaytitle":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Mike McGuire (politician)</span></span>","namespace":{"id":0,"text":""},"wikibase_item":"Q19662567","titles":{"canonical":"Mike_McGuire_(politician)","normalized":"Mike McGuire (politician)","display":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Mike McGuire (politician)</span></span>"},"pageid":44341390,"thumbnail":{"source":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/06/State_Senator_Mike_McGuire.jpg/330px-State_Senator_Mike_McGuire.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","width":330,"height":412},"originalimage":{"source":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/0/06/State_Senator_Mike_McGuire.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","width":1165,"height":1456},"lang":"en","dir":"ltr","revision":"1381923970","tid":"110e8a49-d097-11f1-b934-b206c161e6d7","timestamp":"2026-10-25T17:11:07Z","description":"American politician (born 1979)","description_source":"local","content_urls":{"desktop":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mike_McGuire_(politician)","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mike_McGuire_(politician)?action=history","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mike_McGuire_(politician)?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Mike_McGuire_(politician)"},"mobile":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mike_McGuire_(politician)","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:History/Mike_McGuire_(politician)","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mike_McGuire_(politician)?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Mike_McGuire_(politician)"}},"extract":"Mike McGuire is an American politician who has been a member of the California State Senate representing the 2nd district since 2014. A Democrat, he served as majority leader from 2022 to 2024 and senate president pro tempore from 2024 to 2025. His district encompasses the North Coast region, from Marin County to Del Norte County.","extract_html":"<p><b>Mike McGuire</b> is an American politician who has been a member of the California State Senate representing the 2nd district since 2014. A Democrat, he served as majority leader from 2022 to 2024 and senate president pro tempore from 2024 to 2025. His district encompasses the North Coast region, from Marin County to Del Norte County.</p>"}